# Ignore virtual environments
**/.venv/
**/env/
**/venv/

# Ignore Python cache and logs
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.log
app_test.log
app.log

# Ignore user uploads (large video files)
**/uploads/

# OS generated files
.DS_Store

env/
.env

# Ignore downloaded validation datasets (100GB+ of real video data —
# never belongs in git; see README's Validation section for where to
# re-download each one, they're all free/public or free-account sources).
# Keep the small evidence/derived files though: manifest.csv, the
# validation run logs, and any reference scripts/docs that came with a
# dataset — those are what actually need to survive, not the raw videos.
test/dataset_1/
test/dataset_2/
test/ubfc_phys/
test/rPPG-10/
test/*.avi
test/*.mp4
test/*.mov
test/*.npy
test/*.zip
!test/*.log

# Ignore the windowed ML-correction dataset (41MB, fully reproducible via
# `python scripts/build_ml_dataset.py test/ --out test/ml_dataset.csv`
# against the real videos above) — same reasoning as the raw datasets:
# derived, regenerable, too big for git. The trained models it produced
# (models/) and the logs proving what it measured (test/*.log) are the
# actual evidence and are kept.
test/ml_dataset.csv
test/ml_dataset_subset_check.csv
